# SELFHOST.RUN — acceptance build driver script (HobbyOS self-hosting,
# wave 2).  Read and executed in-OS by SELFHOST.BIN (src/user/selfhost/).
#
# One stage per line, '|'-separated:  <phase>|<tool>|<args...>
#   <phase> is the acceptance Sx-name used in the [SELFHOST] markers
#           (acceptance.md §1: phase=s0-check-start ... phase=s3-disk-done);
#   <tool>  is the tool's 8.3 binary name, resolved against /TOOLS, then
#           /BOOT, then / (uppercased, .BIN appended when absent);
#   <args>  is passed verbatim to the tool.
#
# w4-src: every stage runs the in-OS GNU make THROUGH the in-OS shell
# (SH.BIN + /SRC/SELFHOST.SH) so the build runs with cwd=/SRC.  The driver
# itself spawns tools from cwd "/" — every HobbyOS process starts with
# cwd=/ (src/kernel/process.c) — and `make -f Makefile.hobbyos <target>`
# needs the /SRC working directory for its relative src/... references
# (the frozen acceptance command).  SELFHOST.SH does `cd /SRC` then
# `/TOOLS/MAKE.BIN -f Makefile.hobbyos "$1"`; sh script mode + the cd
# builtin + external execution are all proven (sh.c script mode, builtits).
#
# The stages mirror acceptance.md S0..S3 (the in-OS build).  S4/S5 are host
# side (extract OUT.IMG and boot it) and belong to the verify loop, not this
# script.
s0-check|SH.BIN|/SRC/SELFHOST.SH check
s1-user|SH.BIN|/SRC/SELFHOST.SH user
s2-kernel|SH.BIN|/SRC/SELFHOST.SH kernel
s3-disk|SH.BIN|/SRC/SELFHOST.SH disk
